# Men's Diamond Eternity Band: 4 Prong Issues Fail at Year 5

[![Men's diamond eternity band guide — 4 prong failure modes, full vs half, channel-set security explained](/images/mens-diamond-eternity-band-featured.jpg "Men's Diamond Eternity Band: 4 Prong Issues Fail at Year 5 — DiamondCritics")](https://www.bluenile.com/wedding-rings/mens-wedding-rings/diamond?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=Image)

## TL;DR — Men's Diamond Eternity Band in One Scroll

**A men's diamond eternity band is not a standard wedding band with extra diamonds. The setting type determines whether the ring lasts 30 years or starts losing stones at year 4.**

**The 4 issues that fail at year 5:**
1. **Shared Prong Drift** — shared prong tips wear flat by year 3–5; adjacent stones loosen simultaneously.
2. **Channel Wall Undercutting** — machine-pressed channel walls under 0.5mm crack under lateral impact; stone shifts inward.
3. **Full Eternity Rotation Wear** — a loose full eternity rotates; the top-of-finger zone absorbs all impact; those settings fail first.
4. **14k White Gold Prong Softening** — rhodium wears off prong tips by year 2; bare 14k gold thins by year 5; platinum lasts 15+ years.

