## Metal Comparison — Best Metal for a Men's Diamond Eternity Band

| Metal | Prong Hardness | Rhodium Needed | 5-Year Prong Status | Price Multiplier | What this means |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 14k White Gold | 155 HV | Yes — every 18–24mo | Tips thin; re-tip at year 5 | 1× | Most popular; needs maintenance |
| 14k Yellow Gold | 150 HV | No | Tips thin; visible at year 5 | 1× | Warm tone; same maintenance gap |
| 14k Rose Gold | 175 HV | No | Copper alloy resists thinning | 1× | Hardest gold alloy; best 14k choice |
| Platinum | 160 HV | No (naturally white) | Tips intact at year 15+ | 1.9× | No replating; best long-term choice |
| **What this means** | Harder = slower wear | No rhodium = no stripping | Platinum prong tips last longest | Skip 18k | Rose gold or platinum for active men |

**Verdict:** 14k rose gold is the best gold alloy for a men's eternity band. The copper content slows prong tip wear better than 14k white or yellow gold.

Platinum is better still — no rhodium, no stripping, prong tips last 15+ years. See the [platinum vs. white gold comparison](/round-diamond-platinum-vs-white-gold) for the full cost-over-time breakdown.

