## Pros and Cons: Men's Diamond Eternity Band

### Pros

- **Full-finger sparkle at every angle.** A full eternity band creates 360° of diamond visibility. The [Bold Diamond Eternity at $4,305](https://www.bluenile.com/wedding-rings/bold-diamond-eternity-ring-in-14k-white-gold-7-mm-1-2-ct-tw-item-147439?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) with 1/2 ct looks substantial from every viewing angle. No other men's band style matches this.
- **Burnished setting removes all prong risk.** The [Milgrain Burnished Set at $3,590](https://www.bluenile.com/wedding-rings/milgrain-burnished-set-diamond-wedding-ring-in-14k-white-gold-5-mm-1-5-ct-tw-item-150698?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) has 1.5 ct of diamonds set flush with the band. No prong tips. No snagging. 1.5 ct at $3,590 represents excellent value per carat.
- **More diamond weight per dollar.** Eternity bands distribute diamond weight across the full band. You get more total carat weight for less than a single solitaire at the same price. See the [men's diamond engagement ring guide](/mens-diamond-engagement-ring) for the per-carat cost comparison. If you want a step-cut solitaire alongside the eternity band, the [men's emerald cut ring guide](/mens-emerald-cut-ring) covers that combination directly.
- **Metal choice removes all maintenance.** Choosing platinum eliminates rhodium replating. Choosing burnished setting eliminates prong inspections. The [Milgrain Burnished Platinum at $5,035](https://www.bluenile.com/wedding-rings/milgrain-burnished-set-diamond-wedding-ring-in-platinum-5-mm-1-5-ct-tw-item-150704?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the only ring in this guide that requires zero maintenance at year 5, year 10, and year 20.

### Cons

- **Full eternity cannot be resized.** Diamonds go all the way around — there is no plain metal section to cut. If your ring size changes, you need a replacement band. Plan for this before purchasing.
- **Shared prong settings require annual inspection.** Any shared prong eternity band — including the [Milgrain Vertical Row at $2,880](https://www.bluenile.com/wedding-rings/milgrain-vertical-row-diamond-eternity-ring-in-14k-white-gold-7-mm-3-8-ct-tw-item-288422?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — needs a professional check every 12 months. This costs $50–$100 per visit. Skip it and you risk silent prong drift.
- **Full eternity + active lifestyle = uneven wear.** The rotation problem (Issue 3 above) means active men who choose full eternity will see wear at 12 o'clock before 6 o'clock. This is cosmetic at first, structural by year 7.
- **Palm-side comfort tradeoff.** Diamonds on the palm side press against adjacent fingers during grip. Most men adjust, but some find it distracting during heavy lifting or grip-intensive work.

