**Farzana Hasan, diamond expert** | [About Farzana](/about-farzana/)

The 4 prong issues are not scare tactics. They are what I see in my inspection work every year. Shared prong drift at year 4.

Channel wall cracks in underweight settings. Prong tips worn flat on 14k white gold bands not replated since purchase.

Every one of these failures is preventable.

Choose channel or burnished at entry. Add milgrain borders if you want shared prong. Choose platinum if you want to never think about maintenance.

